// EXPECT-DIAG: Variable 'k' is declared but never used
// EXPECT-NO-DIAG: Variable 'k' is assigned but the value is never read
// LEC-005: a variable that is never read at all used to be reported twice --
// "declared but never used" AND "assigned but never read (dead store)" for its
// own initializer -- the same finding with two hints. The never-used warning
// is the one that says what to do about it; the dead-store warning is kept
// for variables that ARE read somewhere (see 15_dead_store_in_loop.tr and
// 43_...).
fn main(): int {
    immut k: int = 5;
    return 0;
}
